\1\n    <div id="site-header"></div>
    <!-- Header -->
    
    <main class="lesson-container py-4">
        <!-- Breadcrumb -->
        <div id="tutorial-header"></div>
        
        <div class="content lesson-content" style="font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--text-secondary);">
            <p>Traceroute is a utility that records the route (the specific gateway computers at each hop) through the internet between your computer and a specified destination computer.</p><h3>Why Use It?</h3><p>While ping tells you IF a destination is reachable, traceroute tells you WHERE the connection fails along the path.</p><h3>Related Command</h3><p>Use <a href='../../commands.html' class='cmd-badge' style='display:inline-block'>tracert</a> (Windows) or <code>traceroute</code> (Linux) to map the network path.</p>
        </div>
        
        <!-- Navigation -->
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color); padding-top: 1.5rem; margin-top: 3rem;">
